# Context filter for containers/Dockerfile.target (read by podman and docker).
#
# The target image now takes the WHOLE repository (COPY . ./), because the
# previous curated COPY list rotted exactly the way curated lists do here:
# tests added after the list was written read .gitignore, LICENSE, REUSE.toml
# and .github/, none of which were in the image, and every container job went
# red while local runs -- which mount the full tree -- stayed green.
#
# So this file lists only what must NOT reach the image, and each entry says
# why. Unlike .gitignore, a bare name here matches at the context ROOT only,
# so `reference` does not touch docs/reference/ (a test asserts it is there).
#
# .git       -- tests that need a worktree already skip without one; shipping
#               history into six images per push buys nothing.
# reference  -- gitignored 264MB local sweep data; never in CI checkouts but
#               present on dev machines, and a local build must match CI.
# vendor     -- gitignored extracted upstream trees, same reason.
.git
reference
vendor
**/__pycache__
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
